    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is headlined by **Corbin Carroll**, who registers an elite 82.01 score. Facing a middle-of-the-road xERA in Sandy Alcantara, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and an optimal #5 spot in the order, making him our primary candidate for both production and the stolen base upside we prioritize. **Mickey Moniak** (73.71) and **Seiya Suzuki** (64.79) round out our top-tier plays; **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a breakout performance thanks to a massive +14% park factor boost, while **Seiya Suzuki** maximizes his value batting second against a vulnerable matchup. Meanwhile, **Griffin Conine** remains a high-upside play at 61.48; despite the looming threat of a high-strikeout arm in Burnes, his strong 0.371 xwOBA and favorable platoon split keep him firmly in the green.\n\nOur toughest roster decision centered on **Cole Young**, who landed just outside the threshold with a 39.66 score. While his elite catcher-defensive suppression metrics and the favorable stolen base environment created by a slow-working pitcher provided a slight bump, the optimizer favored the higher raw projection and park-adjusted scoring of **Zach McKinstry** and **Jose Caballero**. Though both struggle with defensive suppression and platoon headwinds, their volume in the lineup remains the safer bet for Roto efficiency. We are also closely monitoring **Moises Ballesteros** and **Josh Naylor**; both are currently reliant on assumed lineup spots. **Josh Naylor** faces a difficult matchup against the 3.32 xERA of Reid Detmers, and any shift in the order could push his marginal 46.17 score further toward our 40.0 floor, necessitating a quick pivot to our bench depth if the confirmed lineups shift.",
